@startuml
title Reflective Worker Workflow (reflection and adaptation)

start
:Receive draft and retrieved evidence from LangGraph state;

if (Is the draft empty?) then (yes)
    :Record gap **no_evidence**;
    :Instruction: search again with keywords
    that name the topic of the question;
    :Review verdict = **insufficient**;
else (no)
    repeat :Take the next draft claim;
        if (Claim cites a passage ID?) then (no)
            :Gap **uncited_claim**
            Instruction: find evidence for the claim
            or remove it;
        elseif (Cited passage was retrieved?) then (no)
            :Gap **citation_not_retrieved**
            Instruction: retrieve evidence and cite
            a returned passage, or remove the claim;
        elseif (Support ratio >= 0.60?) then (no)
            :Gap **low_support**
            Instruction: narrow the claim to what
            the passage states (quote the passage);
        else (yes)
            :Mark claim supported;
        endif
    repeat while (More claims?) is (yes) not (no)
    if (Any gaps?) then (yes)
        :Review verdict = **revise**;
    else (no)
        :Review verdict = **pass**;
    endif
endif

:Return review (verdict, per-claim checks,
gaps with instructions) to LangGraph;
note right
  The Reflective Worker does not decide
  the next step. route_after_review()
  in the LangGraph router does.
end note
stop

@enduml
